{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"f35a8f0bc12aba0ec3092a1e024018bcd7fba615164c48c8524c6d973dd1bc58","digest":{"component_or_area":"git subprocess call sites (gerrit_client, workspace)","key_entities":["src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py","src/rebar/opcert_service/workspace.py","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py","_GIT_TIMEOUT","subprocess.TimeoutExpired","GerritError","WorkspaceError","clone_change_ref","workspace._git","tests/unit/test_git_timeout_bounds_77e1.py"],"problem_keywords":["git timeout","network hang","unbounded subprocess call","credential leak","blobless snapshot"],"propositions":["Network-capable git subprocess calls in gerrit_client.py and workspace.py lack explicit timeout bounds, risking indefinite hangs on stuck remotes or credential helpers","subprocess.TimeoutExpired in gerrit_client.clone_change_ref escapes the existing token-redaction handler, creating a credential-disclosure path","gerrit_client.py and workspace.py must bound all git calls with _GIT_TIMEOUT=300 to match the precedent established by bug 747f, routing timeout exceptions through module-specific error types","Two network-capable sites in _commands/init.py and _commands/fsck_repair.py are deferred to task 983f pending resolution of conflicting changes in bug 01e8","The _ref_lock.py module is already fully bounded by its structural requirement that timeout be passed as a mandatory keyword-only parameter"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787641853957217001,"uuid":"f6edf31b-aff1-4d41-9b41-213c79d85937"}